[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:92. Asking for Trouble]
[00:00.540]Passage 92 | 文章九十二
[00:02.650]Asking for trouble. | 自找麻烦。
[00:05.355]It must have been about two in the morning when I returned home. | 我回到家时，大概是凌晨两点钟。
[00:11.465]I tried to wake up my wife by ringing the doorbell, but she was fast asleep. | 我试着按门铃叫醒妻子，但她睡得很熟。
[00:18.010]So I got a ladder from the shed in the garden, put it against the wall, and began climbing towards the bedroom window. | 于是我从花园的小屋里拿了一把梯子，靠在墙上，开始爬向卧室的窗户。
[00:27.650]I was almost there when a sarcastic voice below said, | 我快到那里的时候，下面传来一个讽刺的声音说，
[00:34.405]"I don't think the windows need cleaning at this time of the night." | “我认为窗户在半夜不需要清洁。”
[00:40.230]I looked down and nearly fell off the ladder when I saw a policeman. | 我往下看，当我看到一个警察时，差点从梯子上摔下来。
[00:47.775]I immediately regretted answering in the way I did, but I said, | 我立刻后悔那样回答了，但我还是说，
[00:53.260]"I enjoy cleaning windows at night." | “我喜欢在晚上擦窗户。”
[00:57.500]"So do I," answered the policeman in the same tone. | “我也是，”警察用同样的语调回答。
[01:02.045]"Excuse my interrupting you. | “抱歉打扰你。
[01:04.640]I hate to interrupt a man when he's busy working, but would you mind coming with me to the station?" | 我不喜欢打扰一个正在工作的人，但你介意和我一起去警察局吗？”
[01:12.955]"Well, I'd prefer to stay here," I said. "You see, I've forgotten my key." | “嗯，我宁愿待在这里，”我说。“你看，我忘了我的钥匙。”
[01:19.505]"Your what?" he called. | “你什么？”他喊道。
[01:22.185]"My key!" | “我的钥匙！”
[01:24.240]I shouted. | 我喊道。
[01:26.080]Fortunately, the shouting woke up my wife, | 幸运的是，我的喊声吵醒了我的妻子，
[01:30.755]who opened the window just as the policeman had started to climb towards me. | 就在警察开始爬向我的时候，她打开了窗户。